A||N||6||LokiTheGreenGremlin||Wondering somthing about a 84 Fiero with a blown motor.||||5||
Z||000000||LokiTheGreenGremlin||12-28-1999||06:22 PM||||I'm wondering if $350 is too much to pay for a 1984 Fiero se 4 cyl, with a blown engine and bad paint.  I don't see any problems with the interior. and the car is rather clean...I don't know much about Fiero's...and I don't want to spend money on a fiero with a bad motor and put a lot of money into it, and find out I can get one without motor problems cheaper....lol.  Any help would be appriciated.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||kong||12-28-1999||08:17 PM||||But it!||||reg||12
Z||000002||kong||12-28-1999||08:18 PM||||Sorry wrong key; Buy it!||||reg||1
Z||000003||2FAST4U||12-28-1999||08:57 PM||||That is a good price. The 4 Cyl motor is inexpensive to rebuild and dependable. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sage||12-28-1999||10:46 PM||||Check out the steering rack, wheel bearings, bushings, cradle mounts suspension,everything that isn't the engine. That sounds like  a very good price, if the only MAJOR things you have to do is rebuild a 2.5 and paint the car.  If you have to replace like the rack and ball joints and/or A arms etc, you will eventually have as much in it as you would spend on one that doesn't need all that to begin with.  If the engine is all it needs, I would offer 250.00, but pay the 350.00 if they won't come down.  Never hurts to try, after all, it is obvious that they don't want to put money into it!  Something else to consider, how much of the work that needs done are you going to do yourself?  Dealers are outrageous and any certified mech. is not going to work cheap. The 2.5 is not hard or that expensive to redo, but make sure you magniflux at least the head, and you know you should do the block too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-28-1999||11:04 PM||||That sounds like a good deal.  But it seems like I heard that '85 and up parts don't enterchange with the '84.  I don't know why.  Maybe it's just some parts.  I know that you can't put a 2.8 in an '84 without alot of headaches.  (This comes from Ed Parks)||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||12-29-1999||10:36 AM||||Loki, make sure you check that car out thoroughly for collision and/or corrosion damage.  The Fiero spaceframe is very rust-resistant unless it's bent and straightened.<P>Take it from someone whose first Fiero was a collision-repaired 84...its nice, freshly painted polymer panels hid a spaceframe that was slowly rusting to the ground.  (Hey, I was a gullible dumba$$ college student.)||||reg||1
